#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128928 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3eae4ea-fb38-5efa-843e-783327b82702" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Limit of a Square Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "57abae04-4bc2-5fb4-a5b0-5c0c6c85f955" :question/math-academy-id "e-49" :question/problem "Calculate $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 2} \\sqrt{x-2}$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nf(x)= \\sqrt{x-2}\n$$\n\n. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(2) &= \\sqrt{2 - 2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{0} \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the graph of $y=f(x)$ \"starts\" at $x=2$. Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x)$ as follows:\n\n![](images/a4/a4a64caff7a8b69454ffc8b93a1baad18bf3d93093b3c85a7c4fc3cb9762a2b4.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we notice that the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 2^-} f(x) = \\textrm{DNE}\n$$\n\nwhile the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 2^+} f(x) = 0\n$$\n\nSince the two limits are not equal, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to 2} f(x)= \\textrm{DNE}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128929 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129258 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad10ca6b-d130-559b-a201-15127659de13" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Limit at Infinity of a Square Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "1b850386-4730-512a-8408-932f7b6931b0" :question/math-academy-id "e-50" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\lim_\\limits{x \\rightarrow -\\infty} \\sqrt{3-x}$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nf(x)= \\sqrt{3-x}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x)$:\n\n![](images/d3/d3960d69c67ce1dbf731975ec1058f590ae6cfd61a3c3b04cb5632ce2eaf68aa.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ decreases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to -\\infty} f(x)= \\infty\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128932 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129260 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0631dd0e-a893-5099-8b52-e7a543e7f783" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Limit of a Cube Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "fbac92a0-de6c-556a-8bf1-030401a5df36" :question/math-academy-id "e-51" :question/problem "Calculate $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to -3} \\sqrt[3]{3x-2x^2}$." :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=-3$ into the expression, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nlim_(x → - 3)\\sqrt[3]{3x - 2x^{2}} &= \\sqrt[3]{3(-3) - 2(-3)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt[3]{-9 - 18} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt[3]{-27} \\\\\n&=-3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129023 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f945ef94-171c-5c19-adb3-f496408dc31b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Limit at Infinity of a Cube Root Function"}] :question/id #uuid "97cc7a63-900d-52e8-ad0b-2232309d6335" :question/math-academy-id "e-780" :question/problem "Compute $\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\infty} \\sqrt[3]{x-1}$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nf(x)= \\sqrt[3]{x-1}\n$$\n\nLet's sketch the graph of $y=f(x)$:\n\n![](images/04/0481bb8a4e6058d3cc41069a210f7fc964d861c7071541432aa7422349410431.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ increases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{x \\to \\infty} f(x)= \\infty\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129258 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad10ca6b-d130-559b-a201-15127659de13" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Limit at Infinity of a Square Root Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57936fa8-32dd-5da0-9b2e-b9e751f9ea27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57936fa8-32dd-5da0-9b2e-b9e751f9ea27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575103} :answer-field/id #uuid "89f6d33c-6d77-579b-97c7-a321f8bf3483" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3eaa5b30-a278-5d74-aa62-f0c0942c6bee" :question/math-academy-id "q-303004" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\sqrt{-(x+7)}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\sqrt{-(x+7)}.$ Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](images/fc/fcd2e8fce7bacf19fc5dd4f65dbee568293ed7ee54f7c4542fdb65d85aaba7d8.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ decreases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=\\infty .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129256 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3eae4ea-fb38-5efa-843e-783327b82702" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Limit of a Square Root Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e46ec9d6-8f02-5d8f-9894-f1b79717a007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e46ec9d6-8f02-5d8f-9894-f1b79717a007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575353} :answer-field/id #uuid "94bf7dd6-1930-5377-b560-90079795f29f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d819e52a-c888-5641-90f2-d3ac6277e69f" :question/math-academy-id "q-337856" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\sqrt{12{x}^{2}+1}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The function $\\sqrt{12{x}^{2}+1}$ is well defined for $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ and so to find this limit we substitute $x=2$ into the above expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\sqrt{12{x}^{2}+1} & =\\sqrt{12\\cdot {2}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129258 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad10ca6b-d130-559b-a201-15127659de13" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Limit at Infinity of a Square Root Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3bde7cc-0467-5c03-b0da-3d4d975316c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3bde7cc-0467-5c03-b0da-3d4d975316c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575323} :answer-field/id #uuid "c33021e9-8a52-56da-aff9-d35ed874340f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575493}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c654afa-cc01-5e40-b594-f3f8e260bef1" :question/math-academy-id "q-337878" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\sqrt{-3x+8}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=\\sqrt{-3x+8}.$ Let's sketch the graph of $y=f(x):$\n\n![](images/26/267253d5390727373450d700edb503e595a8e8fe2bedda6ac93597a1dc9b3e9b.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ decreases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }f(x)=\\infty .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129260 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0631dd0e-a893-5099-8b52-e7a543e7f783" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Limit of a Cube Root Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9f9beaf-1f3f-5ecb-b382-c70b7e9d4750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9f9beaf-1f3f-5ecb-b382-c70b7e9d4750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575250} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0a68138-90e9-5068-a45f-1618bd9b7a35" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ddd96c4-07f2-5b15-8bd6-7a9ad63bd667" :question/math-academy-id "q-337883" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to -3}\\sqrt[3]{7x-6}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We substitute $x=-3$ into the expression, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -3}\\sqrt[3]{7x-6} & =\\sqrt[3]{7(-3)-6} \\\\  & =\\sqrt[3]{-27} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f945ef94-171c-5c19-adb3-f496408dc31b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Limit at Infinity of a Cube Root Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61606271-882c-55fa-afae-9c47c12185ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61606271-882c-55fa-afae-9c47c12185ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575124} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2188212-e382-544c-835c-9192c8bf0f9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/r